                        "entry_id": "5f20999c-e827-3ebe-a858-f3edb9507983",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A young or baby dove."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "35ceccf4-d954-40a4-9dab-950e53c8bb6a",
                                "sense_id": "da27ab0b-e2a1-3d54-96e7-771130caf0cf",
                                "text": "On one of its lower branches was fastened a dove-cote, ingeniously made of willow wands, plastered with adobe, and containing so many rooms that the whole tree seemed sometimes a-flutter with doves and dovelings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b2ad51d-b47b-4c2b-a3b9-2d8b7985af78",
                                "sense_id": "da27ab0b-e2a1-3d54-96e7-771130caf0cf",
                                "text": "She began to wring her hands. \"Oh, my poor doomed dovelings . . . my darling star-crossed daughters . . .\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5f77771-2c8a-4a98-ae1f-339a1a8d2101",
                                "sense_id": "da27ab0b-e2a1-3d54-96e7-771130caf0cf",
                                "text": "Their guan beaks, coupled dovelings, the poorotten, leafing their livers, nieces of the cloud . . . Life! Life! This is life!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
